            <ArticleTitle>[Effects of nicardipine on the functional state of the liver in patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hepatic function was studied in 31 patients with coronary heart disease before and after treatment with nicardipine. Clinical and biochemical findings (enhanced gamma-glutamate transferase and high cholesterol, hepatobiliary syndrome) provide evidence for hepatic function disturbance associated with coronary heart disease. Nicardipine produced a good subjective response, the attenuation of hepatobiliary syndrome. Biochemical indices did not change.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
